//! The `inline-size` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines the
//! size of an element's block along the [inline
//! axis](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Grid_Axis). If the `writing-mode` is
//! horizontal, it corresponds to the `width`; if the writing mode is vertical, it corresponds to the
//! `height`. A related property is `block-size`, which defines the other dimension of the element.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: inline-size of containing block.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Depends on the values of other properties.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <box-size> | <anchor-size()>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-3/#propdef-inline-size
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/inline-size
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

